note long_63: names of exactly 63 bytes, the longest a name may be, are accepted and compared in full:
note two locals that differ only in their 63rd byte hold 3 and 5, and a function of 63 bytes returns 1,
note so the result is 3 * 10 + 5 + 1 = 36.
fn abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijf to int
ret 1
end
